normalized_right_count=-1

propagation=logical positive -> Motor GPIO high -> settled encoder direction gpio51 low/gpio50 high -> raw left negative/raw right positive -> both normalized directions negative
superseded_inference=MotorDevice hardware polarity conversion was initially suspected
inference_invalidated_by=user observed that the five-second PWM3000 window only buzzed and neither wheel rotated, so Encoder direction could not identify physical Motor polarity
current_conclusion=GPIO/PWM producer state was observed, but physical motion did not occur; Motor polarity is unresolved until old/current A/B can be observed after physical board recovery
excluded=PWM channel overwrite; both providers remained enabled at 30 percent duty for the complete window
test_artifact=the prior 20ms destructive reads could sample direction-input transition and falsely accept the wrong polarity
